==Trivia==
*He is based on the ''[[wikipedia:Kappa (folklore)|kappa]]'', an amphibious, reptilian, humanoid ''[[wikipedia:Yōkai|yōkai]]'' with a penchant for cucumbers.
**''Kappa'' is contraction of ''kawa'', meaning "river", and ''wappa'', meaning "child"; these two words together form Kappy Jr.'s Japanese name, Kawawappa Jr.
*His name may be a reference to Kuppa Jr., the Japanese name of the ''Mario'' character [[mariowiki:Bowser Jr.|Bowser Jr.]]
*The first two stages he appears in reference songs:
**[[Flow Like the Stream (Merciless)|Flow Like the Stream]]'s Japanese name, Kawa no Nagare no Yō ni (河の流れのように, "Like the Flow of the River"), is also the name of a [https://youtu.be/_JPKop-dYJ8 song] by [[wikipedia:Hibari Misora|Hibari Misora]], except the stage name spells ''kawa'' (river) with the kanji 河 instead of 川.
**[[Guided by Currents (Merciless)|Guided by Currents]]' Japanese name, Kawa no Nagare ni Mi o Makase (河の流れに身をまかせ, "Give Yourself to the Flow of the River"), is a reference to the song "[https://youtu.be/p3Mi4Ma1eDA Toki no Nagare ni Mi o Makase]" (時の流れに身をまかせ, "Give Yourself to the Flow of Time") by [[wikipedia:Teresa Teng|Teresa Teng]].
*He was the first enemy to have the [[Surge Attack]] ability.
*He is the only Advent Boss to also appear in a different Advent Boss's main stage, spawning in both his own stage, Flow Like the Stream, and in [[Kappy Kawano]]'s [[Ghost King Finale (Brutal)|Ghost King Finale]].

